hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19102","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from a man, from Kab ibn Murra al-Bahzi, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which night is most responsive, and Sufyan once said most heard, he said: The last innermost part of the night."
"19103","And whoever frees a slave, Allah frees for each limb of it a limb of him from the Fire."
"19104","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from a man, from Kab ibn Murra al-Bahzi, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which night is most heard? He said: The last innermost part of the night. He said: Then he said: Then prayer is accepted until the dawn prayer is prayed, then there is no prayer until the sun is a spear-length or two spear-lengths, then prayer is accepted until the shadow stands at spear-length, then there is no prayer until the sun declines, then prayer is accepted until the sun is a spear-length or two spear-lengths, then there is no prayer until the sun sets. He said: When you wash your face your sins exit from your face, and when you wash your hands your sins exit from your hands, and when you wash your feet your sins exit from your feet."
